Use OH 7.0's ALSA adapter (drivers/peripheral/audio supportlibs, with the hooks of 0005) instead of the port's own
board adapter (fajita/drivers/audio), and start audio_server at boot again.

- The port's adapter installs libaudio_render_adapter.z.so / libaudio_capture_adapter.z.so over OH's. It reads
  alsa_adapter.json in another format ("cardId" a string), opens playback on PCM device 2 and capture on 1 while its
  routes feed the speaker from MultiMedia1 and record into MultiMedia3 (the OnePlus 6T's card), so on the OnePlus 6
  both directions ran on unrouted front ends. fajita/BUILD.gn no longer builds it (the sources stay).
- 0001 stopped audio_server at boot because without a sound card it never answered and SceneBoard's calls into it
  blocked SceneBoard's main thread past 6 s. With the card and the HDI working, it runs.

